Fix two parallel decomposition bugs for partitioned nonconforming tetrahedral
meshes that make results depend on the partitioning: an MPI deadlock and
silently wrong parallel conforming interpolation. Both surface readily when a
serial nonconforming mesh (e.g. saved by a previous AMR run) is loaded and
distributed with an arbitrary (e.g. METIS) partitioning; SFC-based partitions
keep refinement neighborhoods together, which makes the configurations rare
during live AMR.

1. NCMesh::TraverseTriFace only emitted tet edge-face constraints when a
   first-level slave face was split further or belonged to another rank. A
   rank whose elements are attached to an interior edge of the face split
   without owning any slave face (an "edge-only" neighbor) was then invisible
   on the master's owner: the constraint never entered its face list,
   ParNCMesh::CalculatePMatrixGroups omitted the neighbor from the master's
   P matrix groups, and
   ParFiniteElementSpace::BuildParallelConformingInterpolation deadlocked
   (the neighbor spins in MPI_Iprobe for rows that are never sent while the
   remaining ranks enter the collective HypreParMatrix construction). The
   constraints are now emitted unconditionally: TraverseTetEdge only
   registers edges that are MASTER or CONFORMING in the edge list, and
   AddDependencies keeps the first constraint for a DOF, so the resulting
   interpolation is unchanged; the fix also repairs the related GroupId/rank
   confusion in ParNCMesh::MakeSharedList (entity_owner holds GroupIds, and
   group 0 is the singleton {MyRank}).

2. A hanging vertex interior to a master edge/face could be owned (minimum
   rank among elements touching it) by a rank whose elements touch the
   refined region only through that vertex. Such a rank sees the master and
   all of its slaves as ghosts, and BuildParallelConformingInterpolation
   skips ghost slaves when building dependencies, so the owner never
   constrained the vertex and wrongly treated it as a true DOF with an
   identity P row: the global number of true DOFs depended on the
   partitioning (the symptom of mfem#3925) and downstream solves were
   silently wrong. ParNCMesh::BuildVertexList now reassigns each such vertex
   to the minimum rank among the owners of the slaves whose closure contains
   it; every rank touching the vertex sees the same master and slave lists,
   so the assignment is globally consistent, and the new owner constrains
   the vertex through its local slave with the existing dependency code.

